IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc5-s144-to-149.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada): PART IV, the sub-heading "Escapes and Rescues" (sections 144 to 149). Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30). It is not the official text.
-- Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING) or a core type. JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words; NOTHING otherwise.
-- Seams: `s 515 the accused is bound by a release order` (BOOLEAN, taken from ccc20), `s 2 prison: ...` and `s 2 peace officer: ...` (MAYBE BOOLEAN, section 2).

§ `Part IV -- Escapes and Rescues (ss 144-149)`

§§ `s 144 Prison breach`

-- src:2930 | 144 Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who
-- src:2931 | (a) by force or violence breaks a prison with intent to set at liberty himself or any other person confined therein, or
@ref s 144(a) (src:2930-2931)
GIVEN `s 2 prison: the place is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person by force or violence breaks the prison` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts with intent to set at liberty themselves or any other person confined in it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144(a) the person by force or violence breaks a prison with intent to set at liberty a person confined in it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 2 prison: the place is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the person by force or violence breaks the prison` AND `the person acts with intent to set at liberty themselves or any other person confined in it` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2930 | 144 Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who
-- src:2932 | (b) with intent to escape forcibly breaks out of, or makes any breach in, a cell or other place within a prison in which he is confined.
@ref s 144(b) (src:2930-2932)
GIVEN `s 2 prison: the place is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is confined in a cell or other place within the prison` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person breaks out of, or makes any breach in, the cell or other place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts with intent to escape forcibly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144(b) the person confined in a prison with intent to escape forcibly breaks out of, or makes a breach in, a cell or other place within it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 2 prison: the place is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the person is confined in a cell or other place within the prison` AND `the person breaks out of, or makes any breach in, the cell or other place` AND `the person acts with intent to escape forcibly` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2930 | 144 Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who
@ref s 144 (src:2930)
GIVEN `the answer of s 144(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 144(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 144 the person is guilty of an offence under section 144` MEANS
    IF `the answer of s 144(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR `the answer of s 144(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section reaches only the conduct its paragraphs describe

-- src:2930 | 144 Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who
@ref s 144 (src:2930)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 144 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:2930 | 144 Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who
@ref s 144 (src:2930)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 144 the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment WITH
        `mode` IS `by indictment`
        `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`
        `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section states no minimum
        `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section states no fine
        `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section states no fine

-- src:2930 | 144 Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who
@ref s 144 (src:2930)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 144 the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the section states no penalty for the summary limb; section 787(1) supplies it

§§ `s 145 Escape and being at large without excuse`

-- src:2960 | (8) For the purposes of paragraph (2)(a) and subsections (3) to (5), it is a lawful excuse to fail to attend court in accordance with a summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order, to comply with a condition of an undertaking or release order or to fail to appear at the time and place stated in a summons, an appearance notice or an undertaking for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act if — before the failure — the Attorney General, within the meaning of the Contraventions Act, makes an election under section 50 of that Act.
@ref s 145(8) (src:2960)
GIVEN `the failure is a failure to attend court in accordance with a summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order, to comply with a condition of an undertaking or release order, or to appear at the time and place stated in a summons, an appearance notice or an undertaking for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `before the failure, the Attorney General, within the meaning of the Contraventions Act, makes an election under section 50 of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(8) the failure is with lawful excuse because the Attorney General has made an election under section 50 of the Contraventions Act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the failure is a failure to attend court in accordance with a summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order, to comply with a condition of an undertaking or release order, or to appear at the time and place stated in a summons, an appearance notice or an undertaking for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act` AND `before the failure, the Attorney General, within the meaning of the Contraventions Act, makes an election under section 50 of that Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if — before the failure — the Attorney General, within the meaning of the Contraventions Act, makes an election under section 50 of that Act"

