-- src:2962 | (9) In any proceedings under subsections (2) to (4), a certificate of the clerk of the court or a judge of the court before which the accused is alleged to have failed to attend or of the person in charge of the place at which it is alleged the accused failed to attend for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act is evidence of the statements contained in the certificate without proof of the signature or the official character of the person appearing to have signed the certificate if the certificate states that,
-- src:2963 | (a) in the case of proceedings under subsection (2), the accused failed to attend court as required by the release order or, having attended court, failed to subsequently attend court as required by the court, judge or justice or failed to surrender in accordance with an order of the court, judge or justice, as the case may be;
-- src:2964 | (b) in the case of proceedings under subsection (3), the accused was named in an appearance notice that was confirmed by a justice under section 508 and the accused failed to attend court in accordance with the notice or failed to appear at the time and place stated in the notice for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act, as the case may be;
-- src:2965 | (c) in the case of proceedings under subsection (3), a summons was issued to and served on the accused and the accused failed to attend court in accordance with the summons or failed to appear at the time and place stated in the summons for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act, as the case may be; and
-- src:2966 | (d) in the case of proceedings under subsection (4), the accused was at large on an undertaking that was confirmed by a justice under section 508, and the accused failed to attend court in accordance with the undertaking or failed to appear at the time and place stated in the undertaking for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act, as the case may be.
@ref s 145(9) (src:2962-2966)
GIVEN `the certificate is that of the clerk of the court or a judge of the court before which the accused is alleged to have failed to attend, or of the person in charge of the place at which it is alleged the accused failed to attend for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in proceedings under subsection (2), the certificate states that the accused failed to attend court as required by the release order or, having attended court, failed to subsequently attend court as required, or failed to surrender in accordance with an order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in proceedings under subsection (3), the certificate states that the accused was named in an appearance notice confirmed by a justice under section 508 and failed to attend court in accordance with the notice or failed to appear at the time and place stated in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in proceedings under subsection (3), the certificate states that a summons was issued to and served on the accused and the accused failed to attend court in accordance with it or failed to appear at the time and place stated in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in proceedings under subsection (4), the certificate states that the accused was at large on an undertaking confirmed by a justice under section 508 and failed to attend court in accordance with it or failed to appear at the time and place stated in it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(9) the certificate is evidence of the statements it contains without proof of the signature or the official character` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the certificate is that of the clerk of the court or a judge of the court before which the accused is alleged to have failed to attend, or of the person in charge of the place at which it is alleged the accused failed to attend for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act` AND (`in proceedings under subsection (2), the certificate states that the accused failed to attend court as required by the release order or, having attended court, failed to subsequently attend court as required, or failed to surrender in accordance with an order` OR `in proceedings under subsection (3), the certificate states that the accused was named in an appearance notice confirmed by a justice under section 508 and failed to attend court in accordance with the notice or failed to appear at the time and place stated in it` OR `in proceedings under subsection (3), the certificate states that a summons was issued to and served on the accused and the accused failed to attend court in accordance with it or failed to appear at the time and place stated in it` OR `in proceedings under subsection (4), the certificate states that the accused was at large on an undertaking confirmed by a justice under section 508 and failed to attend court in accordance with it or failed to appear at the time and place stated in it`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2968 | (10) An accused against whom a certificate described in subsection (9) is produced may, with leave of the court, require the attendance of the person making the certificate for the purposes of cross-examination.
@ref s 145(10) (src:2968)
GIVEN `a certificate described in subsection (9) is produced against the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court gives leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 145(10) the accused may, with leave of the court, require the person who made the certificate to attend for cross-examination` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a certificate described in subsection (9) is produced against the accused` AND `the court gives leave` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2970 | (11) No certificate shall be received in evidence pursuant to subsection (9) unless the party intending to produce it has, before the trial, given to the accused reasonable notice of his intention together with a copy of the certificate.
