    BRANCH
        IF `the party intending to produce it has, before the trial, given the accused reasonable notice of the intention together with a copy of the certificate` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the party intending to produce it has, before the trial, given to the accused reasonable notice of his intention together with a copy of the certificate"
        IF `the certificate is tendered under subsection (9)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

