§§ `s 149 Service of term for escape`

-- src:2986 | 149 (1) Notwithstanding section 743.1, a court that convicts a person for an escape committed while undergoing imprisonment may order that the term of imprisonment be served in a penitentiary, even if the time to be served is less than two years.
@ref s 149(1) (src:2986)
GIVEN `s 149(2) escape: the offence of which the person is convicted is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the escape was committed while undergoing imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time to be served is less than two years` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 149(1) the court may order that the term of imprisonment for an escape be served in a penitentiary` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 149(2) escape: the offence of which the person is convicted is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the escape was committed while undergoing imprisonment` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- src:2988 | (2) In this section, escape means breaking prison, escaping from lawful custody or, without lawful excuse, being at large before the expiration of a term of imprisonment to which a person has been sentenced.
@ref s 149(2) (src:2988)
GIVEN `the person breaks prison` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person escapes from lawful custody` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person, without lawful excuse, is at large before the expiration of a term of imprisonment to which they have been sentenced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 149(2) escape` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the person breaks prison` OR `the person escapes from lawful custody` OR `the person, without lawful excuse, is at large before the expiration of a term of imprisonment to which they have been sentenced`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means breaking prison, escaping from lawful custody or, without lawful excuse, being at large before the expiration of a term of imprisonment to which a person has been sentenced"
